    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Appian Corp is a public company headquartered in McLean, Virginia, traded under the ticker APPN, and registered with the SEC under CIK 0001441683. On its own site the company describes itself as providing AI automation for the most important business processes at the world's largest organizations, and says it has been automating processes for more than 25 years. Its platform is presented as a way to orchestrate AI agents, systems, and people from a single place, with process automation, artificial intelligence, and legacy modernization as the main product areas. The site lists uses across finance, including AP, AR, invoice processing, and reconciliation, as well as sourcing and procurement, audit and compliance, case resolution, onboarding, order management, and contract review. Appian also says customers can build AI-powered applications without code and embed AI agents that extract data, act autonomously, and generate code from natural language prompts.\n\nThe company states it was named a Leader in the 2025 Gartner Magic Quadrant for Business Orchestration and Automation Technologies (BOAT), and it points to an AI Value Study produced with Harvard Business Review Analytic Services. Among the outcomes it claims for its automation is cutting onboarding time by up to 50 percent.\n\nThe held facts add little beyond the corporate record. No individual lawsuits are listed, and a law exposure count of 131 is recorded for Virginia.",
